==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Master of Logic Mewtone''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Master of Logic Mewtone is a super-backline crowd-controller, kitted with a [[Slow]] that lasts for 4 seconds, maintaining a ~40% uptime. This uptime is increased by his [[Wave Attack|Mini-Wave]], bringing it up to approximately 60% depending on the enemy's distance from Mewtone.

The most notable aspect that sets Mewtone apart from other [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red]]/[[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|anti-Floating]] crowd-controllers is his absurdly high range, coupled with a forward piercing [[Omni Strike]]. These abilities allow Mewtone to strike hyper-aggressive pushers—[[Teacher Bun Bun]] variants, [[Red EnerG]], [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]]s—from a completely safe distance, and lets him pierce far into backlines to hit enemies such as [[Professor A.]] [[Sage Slayer]] extends this usage unto [[Doctor K.O.]], [[Prof. Owlbrowley]] and even [[Sage of Mind Soractes]], serving as one of the only non-[[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] counters to [[Adherence to Virtue]] on higher crowned difficulties.

His [[Conjure]] further expands on this, since it helps you push enemies back should they start pressuring Master of Logic Mewtone, essentially working as a pocket [[Ototo Corps#Breakerblast|Breakerblast Cannon]]. Enemies further away from Mewtone will also maintain a higher uptime on his Slow due to being hit again, meaning this Conjure synergizes incredibly well with the rest of his arsenal, even if it is available only once per cycle and prevents him from being stacked.

The best part about Master of Logic Mewtone likely won't be his crowd-control capabilities (which are still very useful), but rather his raw stats. He deals 37,400 damage per hit (44,880 damage if the Mini-Wave connects on vulnerable enemies) at just Level 30, which is very high considering his massive coverage, allowing him to not only easily snipe super-backliner enemies like [[Camelle]] variants, [[Elder Sloth]], and [[Lowkey]], but also accumulate serious damage to them and their support over time. This damage skyrockets to 59,400 damage per hit (71,280 damage if the Mini-Wave connects) at Level 50. He also has a surprisingly high amount of health for a super backliner (47,600 health at Level 30, 75,600 health at Level 50), being able to reposition up to three times in case enemies start pushing up to him. For the few enemies that do naturally outrange him, they're either too much for him, or usually have enough support for Mewtone to still have viability against them thanks to his Omni-Strike hitting up to 900 range. Being a Special unit too makes him usable in 4-Crown stages, where few snipers are available and super-backliners are effectively non-existent, as he vastly outclasses [[Li'l Nyandam (Special Cat)|Li'l Nyandam]] in every conceivable manner.

Despite how powerful he is, one should exercise caution when using him on stages that have forms of piercing damage, whether it be [[Long Distance]], [[Omni Strike|Omni-Strikes]], [[Wave Attack|Waves]], [[Surge Attack|Surges]], or [[Explosion|Explosions]], as most enemies that have those abilities will be able to easily hit Newtone and bring him down quickly, even with his high health. One should also be careful about [[Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] enemies, as if sent out at an improper time, can directly burrow or revive next to Mewtone and start attacking him.

Overall, Master of Logic Mewtone is an ''immeasurably powerful'' unit that should be upgraded as quickly as possible.

