==Trivia==
*Like [[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|Soractes]], Master of Logic Newtone's Japanese name is slightly different from the historical figure he's based on. In Japanese, the real [[wikipedia:Isaac Newton|Newton]] is ニュートン ''Nyūton'', whereas the [[The Battle Cats|Battle Cats]] character is ニュトーン ''Nyutōn''. It may be a pun on ストーン ''sutōn'' (stone), referencing his [[Sage of Logic Newtone|enemy form]]'s [[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] stone, or 入湯 ''nyūtō'' (taking a hot bath; bathing in a hot spring), since his enemy form is [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] and appears underwater.
**His Japanese name and Red target may also may be derived from the [[wikipedia:Philosopher's stone|philosopher's stone]], a legendary alchemical substance usually depicted as a red stone. [[wikipedia:Isaac Newton's occult studies#Alchemical research|Newton spent decades studying alchemy]] and is thought to have been pursuing the philosopher's stone.
**His Slow ability and [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] target may imply some form of gravity manipulation.
**During his attack animation, the movements made by the spheres that Master of Logic Newtone holds up mirror the movements made by the swinging spheres of a [[wikipedia:Newton's cradle|Newton's cradle]].
**[[Truth's Devouring Maw]]'s Japanese name, Banbutsu Izanau Shinri no Ōuzu (万物誘う真理の大渦, "Great Whirlpool of Truth That Entices All Things"), may be a reference to the Newton quote "I do not know what I may appear to the world, but to myself I seem to have been only like a boy playing on the sea-shore, and diverting myself in now and then finding a smoother pebble or a prettier shell than ordinary, whilst the <u>great ocean of truth</u> lay all undiscovered before me."
**Master of Logic Newtone may have been foreshadowed by the name of the sub-chapter preceding Truth's Devouring Maw, [[Newtown Trench]].
*Prior to [[Version 15.4 Update|Version 15.4]], Master of Logic Newtone and Master of Logic Mewtone lacked the extra ''e'' at the end of their names, matching the real world Newton.
**The change may have been made to add a pun, as Sage of Logic Newtone is Red, in other words a ''new tone''. It may also be a pun on ''stone'' similarly to his Japanese name.
**The change was later reverted in Version 15.4.1, however the name change was reinstated in [[Version 15.5 Update|Version 15.5]].
*Master of Logic Newtone may have been inspired by Abrahamic religions' story of the [[wikipedia:Garden of Eden|Garden of Eden]], as he was added in the same update as [[Temptation's Rhapsody]], Truth's Devouring Maw's Japanese name can be translated as "Great Whirlpool of Truth That <u>Tempts</u> All Things", his enemy form has an apple (the most common depiction of the [[wikipedia:Forbidden fruit|forbidden fruit]]), and eating the fruit gave Adam and Eve forbidden [[:Category:Sage Enemies|knowledge]]. Furthermore, [[Immeasurable Power]] contains [[Angelic Gory]], a fallen [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]], and the serpent that tempted Eve is often associated with [[wikipedia:Samael|Samael]] and Satan, who are fallen angels in many of their depictions.
*The name of the law in Master of Logic Mewtone's Japanese description, にゃん有引力 ''nyan'yū inryoku'', is a pun on にゃん ''nyan'' (meow) and 万有引力 ''ban'yū inryoku'' (universal gravitation).
*Master of Logic Newtone is the only Conjurer whose spirit is completely unable to hit the enemy base. It has 800 range, and Newtone's Omni Strike forces him to stand 900 range away from the base, which, alongside the fact that spirits spawn 150 range behind the caster, makes his conjured spirit narrowly whiff the enemy base by 250 range.
*Master of Logic Newtone's preview shown when entering [[Legend Stages]] incorrectly says "Stage Clear Bonus 11" instead of "Stage Clear Bonus 12"; the actual 11th clear bonus is [[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|Master of Mind Soractes]].
*His target traits, Red and Floating, may be a reference to an apple falling (Red), and gravity itself (Floating).

